# ROM

## Goal

Build a Read-Only Memory (ROM) in Verilog and understand how digital systems use addresses to access stored data.

The purpose of this project is to understand the basic principles of memory before moving on to RAM and Register Files.

---

# What is ROM?

ROM (Read-Only Memory) is a type of memory where data is stored at specific addresses and can be read by providing an address.

The basic operation is:

   Address
      │
      ▼
┌───────────┐
│    ROM    │
└─────┬─────┘
      │
      ▼
   Data Out

The address determines which stored value is returned.

---

# Specifications

| Parameter | Value         |
|-----------|---------------|
| Address Width | 4 bits    |
| Data Width | 8 bits       |
| Number of Addresses | 16  |
| Data per Address | 8 bits |

The number of available memory locations is:

2^Address Width = 2^4 = 16

Therefore, the ROM contains 16 different addresses, each storing 8 bits of data.

